    '<h2 id="arrangement-and-activity-belong-together">Arrangement and activity belong together</h2>\n' +
    "<p>A string's fixed ends constrain its motion. A molecule's connections constrain its collective behaviour. A cell keeps its organization through ongoing exchanges with its surroundings.</p>\n" +
    '<p>Recursive Resonant Geometry, or <strong>RRG</strong>, asks how relationships and activity support one another. Its <strong>geometry</strong> means components, connections, boundaries and constraints. Its <strong>mode structure</strong> means the organized ways those parts change and respond over time.</p>\n' +
    '<h2 id="a-whole-can-become-a-part">A whole can become a part</h2>\n' +
    '<p>In the RRG proposal, compatible active parts may form a persistent whole. That whole can participate in another organization while activity continues inside it. Existing structures can also change the conditions for what happens next: a star makes new reaction conditions; living systems change their chemical surroundings.</p>\n' +
    '<p>The wave introduces a distinction, rather than proving this entire cycle. The examples have different physical mechanisms. The research question is whether a useful, predictive organizing principle connects them.</p>\n' +
